  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Coaching and Teaching in Secondary Education (BS). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] Must make a grade of C or better.\n[grid1 fn2] MATH 140 , MATH 148 , MATH 152 , or MATH 172 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 135 .\n[grid1 fn3] Course selection should meet the International and Cultural Diversity and/or Cultural Discourse graduation requirement, if needed.\n[grid1 fn4] MATH 142 , MATH 147 , MATH 151 , or MATH 171 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 136 .\n[grid1 fn5] Selected in consultation with an academic advisor. Select from history, science, mathematics, or social studies certification. Teaching content electives depend on area selected and should also be selected in consultation with an advisor.\n[grid1 fn6] In consultation with an advisor. Select from INST 301 ; KINE 199 (up to 3 hours), KINE 213 , KINE 216/HLTH 216 , KINE 285 , KINE 305 , KINE 485 , KINE 489 , KINE 491 ; NUTR 202 ; SPMT 285 , SPMT 421 , SPMT 485 , SPMT 489 , SPMT 491 .\n[grid1 fn7] Meets the graduation requirement for writing and oral communication.\n[grid1 fn8] Select from CTSE 312/KINE 312 , CTSE 314/KINE 314 , CTSE 317/KINE 317 , CTSE 321/KINE 321 , CTSE 351/KINE 351 , CTSE 353/KINE 353 , CTSE 355/KINE 355 .",
